The session starts caja with -n so no file manager window appears.  On this
build that is not enough for the desktop: "caja -n" exits with rc=0 without
taking over the desktop even though org.mate.background show-desktop-icons is
true, leaving the user with a bare panel.  --force-desktop makes caja manage the
desktop regardless of the preference state read at startup; -n still suppresses
the file manager window.  Verified on wayfire with the native wayland backend:
icons appear on the first start, no window.

--- a/session/mate-wayland-components.sh
+++ b/session/mate-wayland-components.sh
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 restart_while_running polkit-mate-authentication-agent-1 &
 restart_while_running mate-notification-daemon &
 restart_while_running mate-settings-daemon &
-restart_while_running caja -n &
+restart_while_running caja --force-desktop -n &
 
 #Programs to start once (if we have them), matching Xorg behavior
 nm-applet --indicator &
